# Milestone: M3
# Covers: freezeif(cond) body — freezes body execution while condition holds;
#         reactive re-evaluation when condition changes; Event-based variant.
# defer-to: M5 (requires freezeif keyword, reactive watcher activation, Event type, and ',' runtime)
#
# Reason:
#   'freezeif' is a reactive construct that requires the full reactive runtime
#   (watcher active polling, SUSPENDED state, condition re-evaluation loop) —
#   scheduled for M5.  The fixture also uses the Event type (M6), ',' separator
#   (M5 chk driver), 'every' keyword (M5 reactive), and variable-change watchers.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5+ with reactive runtime and Event type):
# # var x = 1; [00000001] 1
# # freezeif(x == 2) { loop { echo("foo"); sleep(1s) } },
# # sleep(2.5s); x = 2;
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/freezeif.chk)
